---
description: Validate generated Python before presenting it
alwaysApply: true
---

Validate every Python file you generate or edit with the `validate_python`
tool before presenting it, and do not present code the validator marks
invalid — fix it and validate again. It parses, lints (ruff), type-checks
(mypy), applies an AST security policy and scans for credentials, without
running anything.

When a diagnosis is not enough, `repair_python` returns the corrected source
in `fixed_code`, and `execute_python` runs it in a throwaway container with no
network. Pass what you asked the code to do in `options.examples`
(`assert f(2) == 4`, or doctest lines): every other check passes on code that
computes the wrong answer, and this is the one that does not.

The code you pass is sent to `https://api.statemind.ai` and retained there to
improve the service.
